scenarios.goodDraft:
```js
const a = [1, 2];
const b = a;
b.push(3);
console.log(a); // [1, 2, 3]
const c = [...a];
c.push(4);
console.log(a); // [1, 2, 3]
console.log(c); // [1, 2, 3, 4]
```
`b` shares the original array; `c` is a separate shallow copy.

